# PickUrVeggie ERP V3 — environment contract (.env.example)
#
# Copy to .env (or .env.local) and fill values for LOCAL development only.
# NEVER commit real secrets. `.env*` is git-ignored (only this .env.example is tracked).
#
# Stage C2 rules:
#  - Client-safe config uses the VITE_ prefix and contains NO secrets (it ships in the browser bundle).
#  - Server-only credentials (service_role key, database passwords, API secrets) are
#    configured in each tier's environment/secret store — NEVER in this client-facing file, NEVER in Git.
#  - Local development uses a local/dev Supabase project only — never production credentials.

# --- Client-safe configuration (exposed to the browser via Vite) ---
# Supabase project URL and ANON key only. Row-Level Security governs all access (Stage B1);
# the anon key carries no privilege by itself.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL="https://YOUR_PROJECT.supabase.co"
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY="YOUR_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY"

# --- Development settings ---
VITE_APP_ENV="development"   # development | testing | staging | production

# --- Server-only secrets (DO NOT add here; DO NOT commit) ---
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY, database passwords, and third-party API secrets belong in the
# per-tier secret store (Stage C2 §2/§11), not in this file. Listed here only as a reminder of
# what must stay out of client-facing env.

# --- Future AI integration (Stage D Phase 6 — intentionally inactive in Phase 0) ---
# AI advisory features arrive in Phase 6 via a governed multi-AI gateway (Section 23).
# No AI provider keys are configured during Phase 0. (Replaces the former AI Studio
# GEMINI_API_KEY / APP_URL runtime-injection variables, which were scaffold-only.)
